What does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
my $s = "Order 66 shipped to Lot 7";
my @n = $s =~ /(\d+)/g;
say "@n";
```

What does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
my $t = "a-b-c-d";
my $k = ($t =~ s/-/+/g);
say "$k $t";
```

What does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
my $p = "path/to/the/file.txt";
my ($long)  = $p =~ m{^(.*)/};
my ($short) = $p =~ m{^(.*?)/};
say "$long $short";
```

What number does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
my $w = "Mississippi";
my $n = ($w =~ tr/s//);
say $n;
```

What does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
say join '|', split /(,)/, "a,b,,c";
```

What does this program print? (Ignore any trailing space.)

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
my @lines = ('id=7 ok', 'no id here', 'id=9 ok');
for my $line (@lines) {
    $line =~ /id=(\d+)/;
    print "$1 ";
}
print "\n";
```

What does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
my $csv = "  Lagos ;Accra;  Dakar  ";
my @cities = map { s/^\s+|\s+$//gr } split /;/, $csv;
say join ',', @cities;
```
